InterGenOS: show the quick-settings input slider whenever a real capture
device exists, not only while an application is actively recording.

Upstream hides the microphone row until something records; a user who
plugs in a working mic sees nothing and concludes it does not work (the
adoption bar: a capture device the user cannot SEE is not "working").
_deviceItems tracks real input devices (monitors are never listed), and
device add/remove already calls _sync(), so visibility follows hotplug
with no extra wiring. The upstream recording heuristic is kept as a
fallback so a recording stream still reveals the row on a configuration
whose device list is empty.

--- a/js/ui/status/volume.js
+++ b/js/ui/status/volume.js
@@ -419,7 +419,14 @@
     }
 
     _shouldBeVisible() {
-        return super._shouldBeVisible() && this._showInput;
+        // InterGenOS: a capture device the user cannot see is not
+        // "working" — show the input row whenever at least one real
+        // input device exists (the Windows/macOS mental model), not
+        // only while an application is recording. The upstream
+        // recording check remains as a fallback for configurations
+        // with a recording stream but an empty device list.
+        return super._shouldBeVisible() &&
+            (this._deviceItems.size > 0 || this._showInput);
     }
 });
 
